{#
  The bridge's Python modules, one flat key per autofix_bridge_modules entry, which the
  Deployment mounts back at each entry's `path` under /app.

  Rendered here rather than staged on the node and applied by a task (D5's imperative-ConfigMap
  row), so the ConfigMap is part of this role's manifests: under Ansible a module edit changes
  the render and the shared role's rollout restart rolls the pod; under Flux the renderer's
  `checksum/restart` hashes this ConfigMap into the Deployment's pod template.
  scripts/renderer/tests/test_renderer_autofix_bridge_script.py holds both halves.

  The modules live in files/ and in two other roles, never in templates/, because
  validate/k8s_manifests.py renders every *.j2 under templates/ as a manifest. `lookup('file')`
  strips trailing whitespace, and the `|` block puts back exactly one newline, so each key
  equals its source file's bytes.

  Keep comments at column 0 and above the document: an indented comment between two keys would
  land inside the preceding block scalar.
#}
---
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: autofix-bridge-script
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
data:
{% for item in autofix_bridge_modules %}
  {{ item.name }}: |
{{ lookup('file', item.src) | indent(4, true) }}
{% endfor %}
